BEGIN:VCALENDAR
VERSION:2.0
PRODID:-//WebMS Intra//Test fixture//EN
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:What this proves: a YEARLY rule that names no month still counts its days across the
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:WHOLE year, as RFC 5545 section 3.3.10 says. "Every Sunday" means every Sunday of the
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:year (52 of them in this window), not just the Sundays of the month the series began in;
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:"the 1st" means the 1st of every month (12 of them), not just one. Both used to come back
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:quietly short - 4 dates and 1 date - which is the worst kind of wrong, because a calendar
X-WEBMS-FIXTURE-NOTE:with some of its dates missing looks exactly like a calendar with no dates missing.
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:yearly-byday-1@fixtures.webms.test
DTSTAMP:20260901T090000Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20260906T100000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20260906T110000
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY;BYDAY=SU;COUNT=60
SUMMARY:Every Sunday of the year
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:yearly-bymonthday-1@fixtures.webms.test
DTSTAMP:20260901T090000Z
DTSTART;TZID=Europe/London:20260906T140000
DTEND;TZID=Europe/London:20260906T150000
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY;BYMONTHDAY=1;COUNT=30
SUMMARY:The first of every month
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
